      <item>
        <title>RT by @hwchase17: your agent reads your wiki but so does your team. only one of them is fine with english only. openwiki v0.2.4 ships multilingual support. openwiki --update --language &lt;locale&gt; translates the wiki you already have then writes new docs in that language. same flag on --init if you&apos;re starting fresh. see it in action 👇</title>
        <dc:creator>@colifran_</dc:creator>
        <description><![CDATA[<p>your agent reads your wiki but so does your team. only one of them is fine with english only.<br>
<br>
openwiki v0.2.4 ships multilingual support. openwiki --update --language &lt;locale&gt; translates the wiki you already have then writes new docs in that language. same flag on --init if you're starting fresh.<br>
<br>
see it in action 👇</p>
<a href="https://nitter.net/colifran_/status/2082851209069678894#m">
<br>Video<br>
  <img src="https://nitter.net/pic/amplify_video_thumb%2F2082710802981928960%2Fimg%2FyyBpxLthwP3HIgox.jpg" style="max-width:250px;" />
</a>]]></description>
        <pubDate>Thu, 30 Jul 2026 15:30:00 GMT</pubDate>
        <guid isPermaLink="false">2082851209069678894</guid>
        <link>https://nitter.net/colifran_/status/2082851209069678894#m</link>
      </item>
      <item>
        <title>RT by @hwchase17: New version of the eval-engineering skill released, thanks for everyone&apos;s feedback on the first version. npx skills add https://github.com/langchain-ai/langchain-skills --skill eval-engineering updates: - now supports simulating users in multi-turn evals with instructions + examples - more guidance on good Environment Design. examples on simulating backends/databases + how to use traces to make sure the env reflects prod - more instructions on iteratively refining the harness, environment, and verifier with the user Evals/Environments are hard, pls keep the feedback coming, more coming to reduce the friction of doing this while keeping domain experts in the loop!</title>
        <dc:creator>@Vtrivedy10</dc:creator>
        <description><![CDATA[<p>New version of the eval-engineering skill released, thanks for everyone's feedback on the first version.<br>
npx skills add <a href="https://github.com/langchain-ai/langchain-skills">github.com/langchain-ai/lang…</a> --skill eval-engineering<br>
<br>
updates:<br>
- now supports simulating users in multi-turn evals with instructions + examples<br>
- more guidance on good Environment Design.  examples on simulating backends/databases + how to use traces to make sure the env reflects prod<br>
- more instructions on iteratively refining the harness, environment, and verifier with the user<br>
<br>
Evals/Environments are hard, pls keep the feedback coming, more coming to reduce the friction of doing this while keeping domain experts in the loop!</p>
<hr/>
<b>Link</b><br>
<a href="https://github.com/langchain-ai/langchain-skills">
